G5 feat023-r1 - fig-U3-4.ur.svg / .ur.dark.svg marginal bbox graze: pixel-level ink analysis

Finding: the rendered-DOM bbox instrument (fig-text-overlap-ur.log, negative-control
validated) reports ONE bounding-box intersection across the 20 Urdu figure variants:
fig-U3-4.ur.svg and fig-U3-4.ur.dark.svg, left-side annotation header "طرزِ عمل"
(class h, x=245 anchor=end, baseline y=116) against its own annotation line
"پیغام: میرے پاس آنا محفوظ ہے" (class m, baseline y=132): xOverlap 76.9px,
yOverlap 1.2px.

Analysis: 3x standalone render (fig-U3-4.ur-standalone-3x.png), crop x 560-780,
y 300-430 (the right-aligned overlap zone), greyscale raw row profile
(threshold < 160 = ink). The constant 6-ink-pixel column across all rows is the
concentric band boundary arc, not text. Text ink rows:

- line 1 ("طرزِ عمل"): heavy ink rows 328-347 (3x), descender tail to row 364
- clean gap: rows 365-370 contain ONLY the band-arc pixels, zero text ink
  (6 rows at 3x = 2.0px at 1x)
- line 2 ("پیغام: ..."): first text ink at row 371, heavy from row 384

Conclusion: the two lines' glyph ink does not touch. The 1.2px bounding-box
overlap is Nastaliq line-box padding, not ink contact. Recorded as an advisory
observation (tight but legible line spacing in the annotation stack of the Urdu
fig-U3-4 variants, both light and dark); not a defect requiring repair. The
English fig-U3-4 has the same 16px baseline pitch and was measured clean by the
G3 feat023-r2 run; the Urdu Nastaliq line boxes are simply taller.

